# Falling branch, native 32x16 frames: resting on the trunk, rustling tell, sagging tell, falling. resting and rustle
# carry the at-rest cue (#361, D71): a pale raw-wood band round the joint, cut by an ink zig-zag, and a chip under it.
# Joint (D122, D130, 2026-11-24): on the trunk (resting, rustle, sag) the root (columns 0-5) ramps through a half step (5 6 7) into
# the trunk's bark (1 2 3 4) and flares into a collar, with no ink line down the joint; the raw-wood crack band (cols 6-11, h and
# its zig-zag) stays the D71 cue beside it. falling keeps its broken end: it is off the trunk. Keys 1-7 are kept out of the rim.
